* SUBMIT - RUN A CP/M BATCH FILE

SYSOP ONLY. Private utility; use the local sysop console.

A - Purpose, syntax and examples

:A
* SUBMIT - RUN A CP/M BATCH FILE

SYSOP ONLY. Private utility; use the local sysop console.

Syntax:
    A0:SUBMIT filespec [arguments]

Reads commands from a SUB batch file. Example in a private test: A0:SUBMIT
I0:TEST.SUB

Batch lines can execute programs and change files. Parameters such as $1
are supplied by the arguments. Inspect the whole file and stop on
unexpected prompts. This is the CP/M batch facility, separate from ARUNZ
text aliases and compiled startup aliases.

See HELP COMMANDS for the command index.
